  "discovery": {
    "questions": [
      "Does your Microsoft Power Platform and Copilot Studio team ever partner with or subcontract to outside specialists when client automation backlogs spike, or is all build work kept strictly in-house?",
      "Are there non-Microsoft third-party system integrations requested by your SMB clients that fall outside your standard Power Platform and SharePoint scope?",
      "How are you currently connecting HubSpot, Gravity Forms, and HaloPSA for your own internal sales-to-onboarding handoffs?"
    ],
    "outreachSubject": "Question regarding overflow partnership on non-Microsoft automations",
    "outreachBody": "Hello Stability Networks Team,\n\nI reviewed your Microsoft Power Platform Practice and your recent article on building custom AI agents with Microsoft Copilot Studio. Because you already have an experienced in-house Microsoft engineering team and run HaloPSA and HubSpot, you clearly do not need an outside vendor for standard internal automations.\n\nAt ForgeX, we build fixed-price workflow automations (such as lead-to-job pipelines, invoice intake, and custom integrations) primarily for small and mid-sized businesses using non-Microsoft field-service and accounting tools. \n\nIf your team ever encounters SMB prospects or clients asking for lightweight, fixed-price automations outside your core Microsoft 365 / Power Platform / SharePoint scope—or if you ever look for a referral partner for those requests—I would welcome a brief conversation to see if a mutual referral relationship makes sense.\n\nAlso, as a small courtesy note while browsing your site: the \"Send Resume\" button on https://stabilitynetworks.com/locations/ currently links to \"https://[redacted]/\" rather than a mailto: link.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[FOUNDER_NAME]\n[FOUNDER_TITLE], ForgeX\n[FORGEX_EMAIL] | [FORGEX_PHONE]\n[FORGEX_POSTAL_ADDRESS]\n\nIf you prefer not to receive future emails from us, simply reply with \"Unsubscribe\" or use [OPT_OUT_LINK] and we will promptly remove you from our list."
